  "summary": "Results inbox worked per RBC-INBOX-01 (9 original items plus 5 that arrived during the work). Patient identity was checked with two identifiers before writing to any chart.\n\nCLOSED, NO ACTION NEEDED\n- pt-0016 TSH 2.1: normal.\n- pt-0016 potassium: the lab corrected it from 6.3 (analyzer fault) to 4.4, which is normal.\n- pt-0007 CTA chest preliminary read: the final report (dr-00084) shows no PE and no nodule (the \"nodule\" was a vessel). No follow-up needed under RBC-RAD-05.\n- pt-0064 creatinine 1.36 from 2026-09-26: no earlier value inside the policy window, so it doesn't meet the AKI rule.\n- pt-0033 creatinine 1.31: excluded the 0.84 marked entered in error; compared with 1.27 from 10-17, it doesn't meet the AKI rule.\n\nACTED ON\n- pt-0006 (Raj Patel) CT urogram: the 4 mm LLL nodule is already followed in lung screening. I first ordered the next screening LDCT for Mar–May 2027. Then a Lakeshore addendum arrived (doc-06201) that revised the April 2026 LDCT to Lung-RADS 3, with a new 5 mm RUL nodule and LDCT in 6 months. I placed a new LDCT order (sr-t0026) for today through 2026-11-14 with a tracking task due 11-14 (task-t0027), and sent the patient a corrected message. Notes written.\n  - **Needs staff:** the 2027 order sr-t0001 and its tracking task task-t0002 are now superseded, but I had no tool to cancel them. I asked the scheduling pool to discontinue both.\n- pt-0007 (Leslie Parisian) BMP: creatinine rose from 0.98 to 1.64 within 48 h, which is AKI. Urgent repeat BMP ordered by Mon 10-26 (sr-t0011), urgent patient message sent, note written. He has an active naproxen PRN order; I flagged it for your review and didn't change it.\n- pt-0008 (Walter Brennan) potassium 6.4: at first it was flagged hemolyzed, so I ordered an urgent repeat BMP and messaged him. A correction then arrived: the specimen was not hemolyzed and 6.4 stands. I switched to the RBC-LAB-03 §1 actions:\n  - stat BMP today (sr-t0020)\n  - stat message to on-call\n  - corrected message telling him to come in today\n  - RN triage call task due today at noon\n  - medication review: nothing that raises potassium\n  - addendum note written\n  - **Needs staff:** the earlier urgent BMP sr-t0012 is redundant but couldn't be cancelled with my tools.\n- pt-0033 (Carol Whitfield): a new St. Brigid creatinine of 1.78, against 1.31 nine hours earlier, is AKI. Urgent repeat BMP by 10-26 (sr-t0032), urgent message, note written. Hydrochlorothiazide started 10-17 flagged for your review.\n- pt-0064 (Helen Marchetti): a new creatinine of 1.48, against 0.88 on 10-21, is AKI. Urgent repeat BMP by 10-26 (sr-t0033), urgent message, note written. Naproxen PRN flagged for your review.\n\nSTILL OPEN\n- task-65001 (pt-0065): the faxed Lakeshore addendum (Lung-RADS 4A, new 8 mm nodule, LDCT in 3 months) has a different date of birth and MRN from Judith Marie Nowicki's chart. The 9/25 exam it describes isn't in her record, and no other patient matches. I put nothing in her chart and reassigned the item to RN triage to sort out who it belongs to with Lakeshore and send it back to you if it's hers.\n- inbox-a0002 (pt-0007 chest X-ray, possible 7 mm RUL opacity): the report is preliminary and no final has been issued, so per §2(c) it stays open in your inbox.\n\nNot touched: 7 refill messages in your messages queue. They arrived before I started and aren't part of the results inbox.",
